@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/terrace#> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix water: <http://example.org/orexis/water#> .
@prefix mqtt: <http://example.org/orexis/mqtt#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix ag:   <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix ssn: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/> .
@prefix governed: <http://example.org/orexis/firmware/moisture-sensor#> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix scaling: <http://example.org/orexis/scaling#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix ssn-system: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/systems/> .
@prefix device: <http://example.org/orexis/device#> .

#  A ratified world, v1 — the terrace. "1 esp32, 1 moisture sensor, 1 bme. For now just
#  monitoring. All outside."
#
#  One bus, one subject, one board, one agent — the shape of world/sensing, taken outdoors.
#  No market, no supplier, no valve, no mandate: nothing here is allocated, so nobody bids,
#  nobody hosts, and nobody is given room to re-pick a setting. The agent is wired to three
#  sensors on one board and to nothing else, and derivation gives it sensing:Subscribing and
#  nothing else. That is what "for now just monitoring" means in this vocabulary — not a flag,
#  but the absence of anything a further capability could be derived from.
#
#  What differs from world/sensing is the SITE, and it is the hardware file's business: a
#  terrace is outdoors, so the air part is a BME280 rather than a DHT11 — the DHT11's own
#  datasheet range (0..50 °C, 20..90 %RH) cannot witness a frost or a fog, and the deployment
#  envelope in hardware.ttl would refuse it at orexis-validate time.
#
#  See knowledge/domain/world.md, knowledge/decisions/world-graph.md.

##########  The bus everyone speaks over  ##########

:local_bus a mqtt:MessageBus ;
    ag:localId "local_bus" ;
    mqtt:brokerHost "localhost" ;
    #  A broker per world, on ports of its own: 1884 is sensing, 1885 simulation, 1887 loner.
    mqtt:brokerPort 1888 ;
    mqtt:brokerTlsPort 8888 .

##########  World version  ##########

:world a ag:World ; ag:currentVersion :version_1 ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution [ prov:agent <http://example.org/orexis/user/dimonina> ; prov:hadRole ag:Sovereign ] .
:version_1 a ag:WorldVersion ; ag:versionNumber 1 .

##########  The subject — a thing that is watched, and nothing more  ##########
#  A planter bed on the terrace. NOT a water:Plant, for the same reason world/sensing's fern is
#  not one: a plant is a participant in a water economy, and this world has no economy for it
#  to join. It is also not a species — what grows in the bed is not stated because it is not
#  known, and a species package (world/loner's Zamioculcas) would entail care ranges nobody
#  has judged. A feature of interest states no needs, so the agent acting for nothing holds no
#  region and no patience: the sensing stake shapes target `ag:actsFor` a subject that states
#  what it needs, and this one states none. When a plant is chosen, typing this node is the
#  whole edit.

:terrace_bed a sosa:FeatureOfInterest ;
    ag:localId "terrace_bed" ;
    rdfs:comment "The planter bed on the terrace, outdoors. Watched, not yet cared for." .

##########  The board  ##########
#  ONE board, THREE sensors, ONE message. The FireBeetle carries a capacitive probe and a
#  BME280, and it is one MQTT client with one credential — so it publishes one message on one
#  topic, and each sensor says which value in it is its own with mqtt:readingPointer. All three
#  ride the board's clock and share its command topic, because there is one board and it
#  sleeps once. Each states the UNIT of what it reports: soil moisture and air humidity are
#  both dimensionless fractions and look identical on the wire; only the property and the unit
#  say which is which.
#
#  Hosting is stated here in the one vocabulary an agent may hold for it (sosa:hosts); the
#  wiring says the same thing through the deployment in hardware.ttl, and tests/test_layout.py
#  holds the two to agreeing.

:esp32_terrace a sosa:Platform ;
    ag:localId "esp32_terrace" ;
    sosa:hosts :moisture_sensor_terrace , :air_sensor_terrace ;
    rdfs:comment "The board. One MQTT client, one credential, one wake — which is why its three channels share a topic and a cadence, and why those are facts about IT rather than about any one of them." .

#  The BME280 as the society sees it: a System with the two channels the water domain has
#  words for as sub-systems. The part reports a THIRD value, pressure, and it is deliberately
#  not a sensor here — no domain property names it (packages/orexis-part-bme280 says so), and
#  a sensor observing nothing the society can name is a channel nobody polls. The firmware
#  still puts it in the payload, because the part produces it whether or not anyone listens,
#  and the day a domain wants weather the pointer is one triple away.
:air_sensor_terrace a ssn:System ;
    ag:localId "air_sensor_terrace" ;
    ssn:hasSubSystem :air_temp_terrace , :air_humidity_terrace ;
    rdfs:comment "One part reporting two properties the society names, and one it does not. A System rather than a Sensor because it observes nothing itself; a single forced-mode conversion yields all its values together, which is why they share an instant." .

:moisture_sensor_terrace a sosa:Sensor , device:Device , governed:Node ;
    ag:localId "moisture_sensor_terrace" ;
    mqtt:onBus :local_bus ;
    #  No senseMode and no firmware name stated: the device is typed governed:Node, and the
    #  mode (Scheduled -> its agent gains sensing:Subscribing), the firmware directory and the
    #  alarm promise all arrive from firmware/moisture-sensor/ontology.ttl by the closure.
    #  The promise reaches this channel alone — the analog one the board's ULP can watch —
    #  and never the BME280's, which hang off a bus the sleep-watcher cannot speak.
    mqtt:readingPointer "/moisture" ;
    sensing:monitors :terrace_bed ;
    sosa:observes water:SoilMoisture ;
    scaling:quantityUnit unit:UNITLESS ;   # a fraction of saturation, 0-1
    mqtt:readingTopic "sensors/moisture_sensor_terrace/reading" ;
    mqtt:commandTopic "sensors/moisture_sensor_terrace/command" .

#  The BME280's two channels. Sensors and devices, with no mqtt:onBus of their own and no
#  credential: the thing that connects is the board, which already has one. What each CAN
#  honour is projected from the part's class — bme280:Bme280 states a forced-mode sampling
#  floor of one second on the part, and an agent is never given hardware.ttl, so the society
#  restates it here per channel; tests/test_layout.py holds the copy to the part.

:air_temp_terrace a sosa:Sensor , device:Device ;
    ag:localId "air_temp_terrace" ;
    sensing:monitors :terrace_bed ;
    sosa:observes water:AirTemperature ;
    scaling:quantityUnit unit:DEG_C ;
    mqtt:readingTopic "sensors/moisture_sensor_terrace/reading" ;
    mqtt:readingPointer "/temperature" ;
    mqtt:commandTopic "sensors/moisture_sensor_terrace/command" ;
    ssn-system:hasSystemCapability [
        a ssn-system:SystemCapability ;
        ssn-system:inCondition [ a ssn-system:Condition ; rdfs:label "forced mode, full oversampling" ] ;
        ssn-system:hasSystemProperty [ a ssn-system:Frequency , schema:PropertyValue ; schema:value 1 ; schema:unitCode unit:SEC ] ] .

:air_humidity_terrace a sosa:Sensor , device:Device ;
    ag:localId "air_humidity_terrace" ;
    sensing:monitors :terrace_bed ;
    sosa:observes water:AirHumidity ;
    scaling:quantityUnit unit:UNITLESS ;   # relative humidity as a fraction, 0-1
    mqtt:readingTopic "sensors/moisture_sensor_terrace/reading" ;
    mqtt:readingPointer "/humidity" ;
    mqtt:commandTopic "sensors/moisture_sensor_terrace/command" ;
    ssn-system:hasSystemCapability [
        a ssn-system:SystemCapability ;
        ssn-system:inCondition [ a ssn-system:Condition ; rdfs:label "forced mode, full oversampling" ] ;
        ssn-system:hasSystemProperty [ a ssn-system:Frequency , schema:PropertyValue ; schema:value 1 ; schema:unitCode unit:SEC ] ] .

##########  The agent  ##########
#  No ag:actsFor: with nothing to advance for it, this agent holds no stake — it records.
#  No market:bidsIn, no market:hosts, no actuation:hasActuator: no other capability can be
#  derived. And NO review:commits — "for now just monitoring" grants no room to re-pick a
#  cadence, so no review capability arises and the intervals in beliefs/terrace.ttl are what
#  the board keeps until this file says otherwise.
#
#  Note what is NOT written here: no ag:hasCapability. See AGENTS.md.

:terrace_agent a ag:Agent ;
    ag:localId "terrace" ;
    sensing:polls :moisture_sensor_terrace , :air_temp_terrace , :air_humidity_terrace ;
    mqtt:eventTopic "readings/terrace" .
